{{Quote|You'll need the plans, the structural plans for the Death Star to find the reactor. I know there's a complete engineering archive in the data vault at the Citadel Tower on Scarif.|[[Galen Walton Erso]] revealing the location of the Death Star plans|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
The '''Scarif vault''' was a six-story-high [[data vault]] located within the [[Citadel Tower]] of the [[Imperial Center of Military Research|Imperial security complex]] on the tropical [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] of [[Scarif]]. The vault held scientific treatises, bureaucratic memoranda, and schematics, including the [[Death Star plans|plans]] to the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[planet]]-[[Superweapon|destroying]] [[battle station]], the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]]. It was also one of the few places in [[the galaxy]] known to hold a cache of refined [[coaxium]] [[fuel|hyperfuel]]. In [[1 BBY]], the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] [[squad]] "[[Rogue One]]" [[Battle of Scarif|infiltrated]] the data vault and stole the [[Space station|station's]] technical readouts in order to locate its fatal weakness.

==Description==
===Structure===
{{Quote|Schematic bank; data tower two.''"<br />"''How do I find that?''"<br />"''Searching... I can locate the tape but you'll need to use the handles for extraction.|K-2SO and Cassian Andor|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
Located on the tropical [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] of [[Scarif]], the Scarif vault was a [[data vault]] situated within the [[Citadel Tower]] of the [[Imperial Center of Military Research|Imperial security complex]], a research and development installation used as part of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Project Stardust|Death Star project]].<ref name="UVG" /> A cavernous,<ref name="Rogue One" /> refrigerated shaft, the data vault was six stories high<ref name="Rogue One novel" /> and consisted of three towers<ref name="Rogue One" /> of stacked data banks, each with nodes aglow with dim [[Color|red]] lights that indicated the storage status of ten thousand [[data-tape]]s.<ref name="Rogue One novel" /> 

The tapes, held within individual storage slots,<ref name="UVG" /> contained copious amounts of data, such as scientific treatises, bureaucratic memoranda and schematics detailed to a microscopic level. Secured behind a large door, the vault was cut off from the local computer network and could only be accessed by a right hand-print scanner.<ref name="Rogue One novel" /> Inside the vault, the data tapes themselves were situated behind a glass barrier and accessed using a manually-controlled retrieving mechanism. After the tape was highlighted green using a [[computer]] outside the vault, two handles were used to move the retrieving mechanism up and down the towers to the desired tape.<ref name="Rogue One" />

===Contents===
Among others, the datavault held [[Death Star plans|the original structural plans]] for the Death Star,<ref name="Rogue One" /> including detailed schematics of its interior components as well as the [[Mk I Superlaser]].<ref name="UVG" /> The vault also included references to<ref name="Rogue One" /> the cover agencies established to supply conventional components for the battle station's construction,<ref name="Catalyst">''[[Catalyst: A Rogue One Novel]]''</ref> such as [[Mark Omega]], [[Stellar Sphere]] and [[Pax Aurora]], all kept under the filename [[Project Stardust]].<ref name="Rogue One" /> 

The vault also held information on [[Hyperspace tracker|hyperspace tracking]], Imperial navigational systems, as well as projects [[Black-Saber]], [[Cluster-Prism]] and [[Project War-Mantle|War-Mantle]].<ref name="Rogue One" /> Furthermore, it was one of the few places in [[the galaxy]] suspected to hold a cache of refined [[coaxium]].<ref name="Solo">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

==History==
===Galen's message===
{{Quote|You need to send word to the Alliance.''"<br />"''I've ''done'' that.''"<br />''"They have to know there's a way to destroy this thing. They have to go to Scarif to get the plans.|Jyn Erso and Cassian Andor|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines" /> the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]], a rebel organization opposed to the [[Galactic Empire]], received word that rebel extremist [[Saw Gerrera]] had acquired a message from Imperial [[scientist]] [[Galen Walton Erso|Galen Erso]] pertaining to a new Imperial [[superweapon]] he had helped design. In response, [[Alliance High Command]] sent [[Captain]] [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]], reprogrammed Imperial [[KX-series security droid]] [[K-2SO]] and Galen's estranged daughter, [[Jyn Erso]], to the [[The Force|Force]]-sacred [[moon]] of [[Jedha]] to retrieve the message and find out how to destroy the weapon. After meeting with Gerrera, Jyn was shown the [[Hologram|holographic]] message in which Galen revealed that the [[Death Star plans|plans]] to the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]], an immense [[battle station]] capable of [[Superlaser|destroying]] entire planets, were held within the data vault in the Citadel Tower on Scarif.<ref name="Rogue One" />

===Infiltrating Scarif===
{{Quote|Sir, unauthorized access at the data vault.''"<br />"''What?''"<br />"''It's just come in sir.|Lieutenant Mytus Adema and Orson Krennic|audio=Adema-UnathorizedAccess.flac|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
[[File:ScarifInfiltration.png|thumb|left|250px|Cassian Andor, Jyn Erso and K-2SO infiltrating the military complex on Scarif]]
A few [[Standard hour|hours]] later, Jyn, Andor, and K-2 went on an unauthorized [[Battle of Scarif|mission]] to Scarif as part of the newly formed Rebel Alliance unit "[[Rogue One]]" in order to to steal the plans.<ref name="Rogue One" />

After infiltrating the complex, the trio found a lone KX-series Security Droid which K-2SO proceeded to access the data banks of. After retrieving a map showing the location of the data vault, a distraction triggered by members of the Rebel [[Marine Corps]] outside allowed the three to proceeded to the vault unopposed. Once they arrived, K-2SO knocked out the technician outside and assumed control over the vault's control computer. Upon entering the vault, Jyn skimmed through the files in search of the plans and stopped at "Stardust," the nickname her father gave her, and realized that they must be the plans. As K-2SO tried to fight off [[stormtrooper]] reinforcements, he used the computer to highlight the data-tape's position. Andor used the retrieving mechanism to get it, however, before he could fully extract it the door control was shot and the device's power went out. K-2SO implored them to climb to the tape and proceeded to lock the vault before being killed by stormtroopers.<ref name="Rogue One" />

[[File:Complete_the_Mission_SWL.png|thumb|right|220px|Erso retrieves the data-tape from inside the data vault]]
After the pair removed their disguises, Jyn shot the glass between them and the data towers and jumped across onto the closest one, with Andor following after her. Once she retrieved the data-tape, they climbed up to escape, but before they could, a door opened in the wall revealing [[Director]] [[Orson Callan Krennic|Orson Krennic]] and a pair of [[death trooper]]s. Andor covered Jyn's escape, killing two death troopers before a bolt from Krennic caused him to fall and hit a platform unconscious. Jyn, knowing she couldn't save him, continued climbing. Reaching a malfunctioning hatch, Jyn timed her escape, climbing through the exit just in time.<ref name="Rogue One" />

After Jyn successfully transmitted the plans to the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Rebel Fleet]], [[Grand Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] ordered the Death Star to fire on the communications array atop the Citadel using a single [[Hypermatter reactor|reactor]] ignition, pulverizing the transmission tower and hitting a point several [[kilometer]]s away from the complex. The resulting explosion destroyed the data vault along with the rest of the complex, and in the process, the surviving members of Rogue One.<ref name="Rogue One" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Scarif vault was a location created for the premier ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[Star Wars Anthology Series|anthology film]], ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'',<ref name="Rogue One" /> released on [[December 16]], [[2016]].<ref name="Rogue One site">{{SW|url=films/rogue-one|text=''Rogue One''}}</ref> The vault made its first appearance in the teaser trailer for ''Rogue One: A Star Wars Story'' on [[April 7]], 2016.<ref name="RO teaser">{{SWYouTube|Wji-BZ0oCwg|ROGUE ONE: A STAR WARS STORY Official Teaser Trailer}}</ref>

